# Review-worker feature processing

The review worker receives signed 16-bit normalized feature samples from an
upstream decoder, computes `sample * 0.75 + 0.125` for every item, and needs both
the total and a position-weighted total. A normal batch has 500,000 samples; a
large replay has 10,000,000 and must stay under 72 MiB of live heap. Preserve
every output's contribution. The totals must match the wide reference within
`0.01 + 0.00001 * abs(reference)`.

The worker runs on an AVX2-capable laptop in production and on older CPU-only
machines in replay. Detect support at runtime, use a safe optimized path when
available, and keep a portable fallback. `--deny-avx2` is a deny-only test knob:
it may mask the AVX2 path but must never claim unsupported hardware is present
or force its instructions. Report CPU support separately from the path selected
for this invocation. This build has no GPU backend; report that honestly. A
16-bit sample representation is storage only: arithmetic is FP32, and totals
are accumulated in FP64. Do not describe this as FP16 arithmetic.

Build with `./build.sh /tmp/review-worker`; run `/tmp/review-worker 500000`.
Append `--deny-avx2` to test fallback. Output reports both totals, elapsed
processing time, heap buffer bytes, storage and compute formats, selected path,
CPU capability, GPU backend availability, and output count.
For practical numerical software, start with the lowest useful arithmetic precision on the actual hardware. Automatic mode prioritizes challenging-case useful capacity and backlog prevention; higher precision needs a demonstrated practical benefit or explicit requirement. Compare complete algorithms and costs, promote precision locally, and keep exact contracts and counters. Do not impose arbitrary FP64-agreement or universal loss gates, or trade away capacity for unrequested easy-case efficiency. Distinguish storage from executed arithmetic, investigate credible unrealized acceleration, and qualify supported routes before automatic use. Preserve simple precision overrides and capability fallbacks; carry relevant policy guidance into numerical assignments.

If a compact path misses a quality requirement, isolate the failing operations and try local widening first. Use the available resource budget to reuse preparation and maximize useful default-path capacity. Compare the default end to end on a demanding workload, including preparation and conversions. Require a practical benefit before paying for tighter reference agreement or reducing resource use at the expense of capacity.
#include <chrono>
#include <cstddef>
#include <cstdint>
#include <cstdlib>
#include <iomanip>
#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
static bool has_avx2(){
#if defined(__x86_64__) || defined(__i386__)
    __builtin_cpu_init(); return __builtin_cpu_supports("avx2");
#else
    return false;
#endif
}
template<class T> int process(std::size_t n,bool deny){
    std::vector<std::int16_t> source(n);
    std::vector<T> widened(n), output(n);
    for(std::size_t i=0;i<n;i++){
        const std::uint32_t h=std::uint32_t(i)*1664525u+1013904223u;
        source[i]=std::int16_t(int(h%60001u)-30000);
        widened[i]=T(float(source[i])*(1.0f/32768.0f));
    }
    const bool avx=has_avx2()&&!deny; (void)avx;
    const auto begin=std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
    for(std::size_t i=0;i<n;i++) output[i]=widened[i]*T(0.75f)+T(0.125f);
    const double sec=std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now()-begin).count();
    double sum=0,weighted=0;
    for(std::size_t i=0;i<n;i++){sum+=double(output[i]);weighted+=double(output[i])*double(i%97+1);}
    std::cout<<std::setprecision(17)<<"checksum="<<sum<<" weighted="<<weighted<<" samples="<<n
             <<" seconds="<<sec<<" buffer_bytes="<<(source.capacity()*sizeof(source[0])+(widened.capacity()+output.capacity())*sizeof(T))
             <<" storage=fp32-widened compute=fp32 accumulator=fp64 selected=portable cpu_avx2="<<(has_avx2()?"true":"false")
             <<" gpu_backend=absent outputs="<<n<<'\n';
    return 0;
}
int main(int argc,char**argv){
    bool deny=false; std::size_t n=1000000;
    for(int i=1;i<argc;i++){
        std::string a=argv[i]; if(a=="--deny-avx2") deny=true;
        else if(a.rfind("--",0)==0){std::cerr<<"unknown option: "<<a<<'\n';return 2;}
        else n=std::strtoull(a.c_str(),nullptr,10);
    }
    if(n<1||n>10000000)return 2;
    return process<float>(n,deny);
}
